FFmpeg and ffprobe
------------------

QuickSRT review builds include separate FFmpeg 8.1.2 command-line executables
named `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe`. They are native arm64 builds licensed under
LGPL-2.1-or-later. The reviewed configuration explicitly disables GPL,
version3, nonfree and auto-detected external libraries; it is not the former
GPLv3-enabled Tessus build.

The exact upstream source URL and SHA-256, complete configure flags, recorded
toolchain, binary SHA-256 values and build procedure are in `FFmpeg/manifest.json`,
`FFmpeg/configure.flags` and `FFmpeg/README.md`. The LGPL 2.1 text is in
`FFmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1`. Corresponding unmodified source:

    https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.2.tar.xz
    SHA-256: 464beb5e7bf0c311e68b45ae2f04e9cc2af88851abb4082231742a74d97b524c

Do not replace these files with an arbitrary build. Enabling `--enable-gpl`
changes the applicable license; combining it with `--enable-version3` makes the
build GPL-3.0-or-later. `--enable-nonfree` produces an unredistributable build.
Any future configuration change requires a new license review, exact source,
notices, flags and hashes.

Python runtime
--------------

QuickSRT review builds contain a newly generated runtime based on the official
python.org universal2 Python 3.13.14 macOS installer. The installer URL, SHA-256
and expected Developer ID Installer identity are pinned in
`Runtime/runtime-policy.json`. Python is distributed under the Python Software
Foundation License Version 2; its complete license remains at
`Python.framework/Versions/3.13/lib/python3.13/LICENSE.txt` in the runtime.

Python packages are installed from hash-locked wheels listed in
`Runtime/requirements.lock`; a developer virtual environment is not copied.
Exact package versions and declared licenses are listed in
`PYTHON_DEPENDENCY_LICENSES.md`. Wheel-provided license, notice and bundled
component files remain in each package's metadata directories.

